   surface colour (no neon). Cadence matches pro-lock-skeleton (1.4s). */
.sk{position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:var(--bg-2);border-radius:var(--radius-s)}
.sk::after{content:'';position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(100deg,transparent 30%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--t3) 9%,transparent) 50%,transparent 70%);background-size:200% 100%;animation:sk-shimmer var(--fl-shimmer-dur) ease-in-out infinite}
@keyframes sk-shimmer{0%{background-position:200% 0}100%{background-position:-200% 0}}

/* Generic ghost rows reused inside card skeletons */
.sk-line{display:block;height:10px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs)}
.sk-line.w-40{width:40%}
.sk-line.w-60{width:60%}
.sk-line.w-80{width:80%}
.sk-block{flex:1;min-height:56px;border-radius:var(--radius)}

/* Hero greeting line — matches .bento-hero-title line box so no reflow */
.sk-hero-line{height:1.2em;width:min(62%,340px);border-radius:var(--radius-s);margin:0}

/* Bento card ghost — IS a .bento-card so it inherits border/radius/shadow/grid */
.bento-card.sk-card{pointer-events:none}

/* Top-bar / sidebar-footer avatar ghost — circle, never a guest icon */
.sk-avatar{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);flex-shrink:0}
.sk-avatar-name{height:12px;width:84px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs)}

/* Sidebar pinned-nav reserve + row ghosts — hold vertical space so no reflow */
.sk-nav-reserve{min-height:var(--sk-nav-h,0px)}
.sk-navrow{height:34px;border-radius:var(--radius-s);margin:2px 0}

/* Plan chip ghost — neutral until subscription.loading is false (never guesses) */
.sk-chip{display:inline-block;height:14px;width:128px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs);vertical-align:middle}

/* Font-of-the-Day ghost — identical box to .bento-fotd so type fades in with no
   metric shift once verifyFontLoaded() confirms the real face */
.sk-fotd{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;padding:24px 16px 16px;min-height:150px}
.sk-fotd-sample{height:clamp(52px,6vw,76px);width:1.4em;border-radius:var(--radius-s)}
.sk-fotd-name{height:18px;width:120px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs)}
.sk-fotd-meta{height:9px;width:64px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs)}

/* Skeleton→content crossfade layer: skeleton fades out as content fades in over
   the same window, so there is no gap and no jump (boxes are size-matched) */
.bento .sk-layer{transition:opacity var(--fl-reveal)}
.bento.is-ready .sk-layer{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}

/* Name blur-in: the flagship name focuses into place when it's known */
@keyframes fl-name-in{from{opacity:0;filter:blur(6px);transform:translateY(2px)}to{opacity:1;filter:blur(0);transform:none}}
.bento-hero-name-in{animation:fl-name-in var(--fl-reveal) both}

/* FOTD type held behind the reserved box until the real face is confirmed */
.bento-fotd-sample,.bento-fotd-name{transition:opacity var(--fl-reveal)}
.bento-fotd.is-font-loading .bento-fotd-sample,
.bento-fotd.is-font-loading .bento-fotd-name{opacity:0}

/* Reduced motion: skeletons become STATIC space-reservers (no sheen sweep) and
   content is simply present — no transforms, no blur. Preserve the information
   (layout) while dropping the decoration (motion). The global reduced-motion
   rule already zeroes durations; these make the static-ghost intent explicit and
   avoid a 0.01ms shimmer/blur flicker.

   ORPHANED, NOT WRONG — checked 2026-08-26, left in place deliberately.
   The `.sk::after` half is live. The two `.bento` halves are not, for two
   independent reasons, and neither is repairable by repointing:

     1. Nothing renders `.bento`, `.bento-card` or `.bento-hero-name-in`.
        Their page, src/pages/Dashboard.jsx, was DELETED in PR #196 (549c6c6),
        not renamed. The two families that do ship — `grad-bento-` in
        ColorStudio and `landing-bento-` in Landing.jsx — are a naming
        coincidence: these selectors cannot match them, neither declares an
        `animation` at all (their reveals are transitions, already covered by
        the global clamp at the top of this file), and Landing.jsx is itself
        imported nowhere.
     2. The animation the first selector guards was deleted by the same PR.
        Before 549c6c6 the rule at global.css:1158 read
        `.bento.is-ready:not(.has-entered) > .bento-card` with
        `animation: bentoIn ...` plus six nth-child delays. That went; the
        guard stayed. So this half guarded nothing even while the class shipped.

   `.bento-hero-name-in{animation:fl-name-in}` above is still declared, so if
   the dashboard bento is ever rebuilt the guard is correct and waiting.
   Deleting is a founder call, not a drive-by. */
html[data-reduced-motion="true"] .sk::after{animation:none;background:none}
html[data-reduced-motion="true"] .bento.is-ready:not(.has-entered)>.bento-card,
html[data-reduced-motion="true"] .bento-hero-name-in{animation:none}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  html:not([data-reduced-motion="false"]) .sk::after{animation:none;background:none}
  html:not([data-reduced-motion="false"]) .bento.is-ready:not(.has-entered)>.bento-card,
  html:not([data-reduced-motion="false"]) .bento-hero-name-in{animation:none}
}

