/* THE ONLY TEXT IN THIS APP ON A GRADIENT THAT AN ALPHA BUMP COULD NOT FIX.
   [gradient-text-below-aa]: the 1200x630 placeholder label measured 2.99:1
   against the 4.5 it needs at 11px, on rendered pixels with the ink hidden and
   the gradient sampled under the label's own rect. Every candidate, measured
   the same way:
     opaque white ink, gradient unchanged            4.46  still short
     --accent-strong gradient, ink left at 70%       3.97  still short
     --accent-strong gradient + opaque white ink     6.36  ships
     28% black scrim over the --accent gradient      4.48  still short
   So the ground had to move, which is why the item called this a design change
   rather than a colour tweak.

   THE FIRST FIX FOR IT WAS WRONG IN DARK, AND ONLY A RENDERED MEASUREMENT SAID
   SO. Swapping var(--accent) for var(--accent-strong) reads like the obvious
   move and measures 5.35:1 in light -- and 3.41:1 in dark, WORSE than the 2.99
   it replaced was in light. --accent-strong is the darker, readable member of
   the pair in light and the LIGHTER one in dark (#0B5ED7 against #4A90FF): in
   dark it is the fill that steps back, not the ink that steps forward. The
   prefers-contrast work recorded exactly this and it is worth repeating here,
   because the arithmetic in light is right and the conclusion still does not
   travel.

   THE GROUND IS THEREFORE THEME-INDEPENDENT, and that is the real answer rather
   than a workaround. This is a mock of a 1200x630 SOCIAL CARD. The card it
   stands for is drawn by scripts/og-cards.mjs, which scopes its token reads to
   the [data-theme="light"] block on purpose -- a share card is always the light
   brand, because LinkedIn and X do not render it in the author's theme. A
   preview that flips with the viewer's theme is showing something the card will
   never look like. Two literals, from the light accent pair, matching that
   generator's reasoning; measured 5.45:1 light and 5.45:1 dark on the same
   ground #365EE2, because the surface no longer depends on the theme at all.

   The 70% ink went opaque too, and that is worth 1.9 points here on its own.
   #346 removed the same 10% haircut from textColorForBg for the same reason:
   the last tenth of alpha is never free and is almost never a deliberate
   design choice. */
.seo-social-img{height:150px;border-radius:var(--radius-s) var(--radius-s) 0 0;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0B5ED7,color-mix(in srgb,#0B5ED7 40%,#8B5CF6));display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.seo-social-img span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:#FFFFFF;letter-spacing:.05em}
.seo-social-body{padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 var(--radius-s) var(--radius-s);background:var(--bg-2)}
.seo-social-domain{font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-bottom:4px}
.seo-social-title{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t0);line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:3px}
.seo-social-desc{font-size:12px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.45}
.seo-checklist{background:var(--card-grad);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-l);box-shadow:var(--warm-shadow);padding:20px}
.seo-checklist-h{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:var(--t0);margin:0 0 14px}
.seo-check{display:flex;gap:12px;padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.seo-check:first-of-type{border-top:none;padding-top:0}
.seo-check-icon{flex-shrink:0;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;border:1.5px solid;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-top:1px}
.seo-check-label{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t0);margin-bottom:2px}
.seo-check-detail{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.5}
.seo-tabs{display:flex;gap:4px;margin-bottom:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.seo-tab{padding:9px 16px;border:none;background:none;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t2);border-bottom:2px solid transparent;margin-bottom:-1px;transition:color var(--dur-1) var(--ease-standard),border-color var(--dur-1) var(--ease-standard)}
.seo-tab:hover{color:var(--t0)}
.seo-tab.is-active{color:var(--accent-strong);border-bottom-color:var(--accent)}
/* Three tabs at 13px with 16px of side padding need ~396px and had 358, so every
   label wrapped to two lines — "Meta & / SERP" — and a two-line tab makes the
   underline read as a box rather than as a selection. Trimming the type one step
   and the padding to 10px brings the row to ~336px, so all three sit on one line
   at 390px. Not a scroller: three short tabs that FIT are always better than
   three that have to be swiped for, which is the whole argument of
   `.rail-overflow` read in the other direction. */
@media(max-width:560px){
  .seo-tabs{gap:2px}
  .seo-tab{padding:9px 10px;font-size:12px}
}
.seo-faqs{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
