/* Reduced motion: the global rule (top of file) already collapses transitions
   and animations; we additionally drop the scroll-snap so motion-sensitive
   users aren't pulled by the rail.

   ORPHANED, NOT WRONG — checked 2026-08-26, left in place deliberately.
   Nothing renders `.dsc-rail-track`, so all four of its rules are dead: the
   base rule above, the `max-width:480px` override, and both halves of this
   guard. Confirmed in a browser on the built app — absent on /discover at 390,
   900 and 1440px, as is the whole `.dsc-featured` / `.dsc-feat-` family it
   belongs to. Its component, src/components/discover/FeaturedRail.jsx, was
   DELETED in PR #196 (549c6c6) along with five other Discover components; the
   stylesheet block outlived it. There is no element to repoint at: no other
   `.dsc-` selector declares `scroll-snap-type`.

   Left rather than deleted because it is the only written record that this
   rail was meant to be guarded — and the reasoning above it is what the two
   rails that DO ship were missing. Those are now guarded (see
   `.plb-toolbar-group:last-child` and `.ggn-presets`, and
   tests/user-sim/27-motion-guards.spec.js). Deleting is a founder call.
   Note the base rule is `x mandatory`, the only one in the file — the four
   live rails are all `x proximity`. */
html[data-reduced-motion="true"] .dsc-rail-track{scroll-snap-type:none}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  html:not([data-reduced-motion="false"]) .dsc-rail-track{scroll-snap-type:none}
