/* cpk — THE colour input for this app (src/components/ColorPickerPop.jsx).
   It replaces the OS-native colour dialog on EVERY surface that picks a colour;
   the component header carries the call-site inventory and the emit contract.

   The panel's SKIN — background, border, radius, elevation, entry motion, edge
   flipping, max-height and scroll containment — comes from the shared `.pop`
   block at the END of this file, because the element carries both classes.
   Nothing here restates any of it. What lives here is only what is particular
   to a colour picker: the instrument, the value row and the swatch sections.
   The one property that has to beat `.pop` is written as `.pop.cpk-pop`, so it
   wins on specificity from this block rather than having to move to the end of
   the file and away from its siblings. */
.cpk-wrap{position:relative;flex:0 0 auto}
