/* Icon controls are icon-only at rest and EXPAND to hold their own label.
   The label lives in the button's normal flow, so the BUTTON grows and the
   text is always inside the button's own box — it never paints over the
   control beside it. Its siblings are pushed along, which is the honest
   reading of the gesture: the control got bigger.

   Width comes from the css-conventions 0fr→1fr track (see
   css-conventions.md → Motion), so the curve runs to the label's REAL text
   width instead of an invented ceiling — that is what makes --ease-entrance
   read correctly here. `.plb-lbl-i` carries overflow:hidden;min-width:0 so
   the 0fr track is allowed to collapse all the way to zero. Padding is
   animated alongside the track because a border-box element cannot narrow
   past its own padding.

   (History: this label used to be position:absolute. #202 fixed the sizing
   half of that — an abspos box with only `left` set has an indefinite inline
   size, so `1fr` resolved to 0px and the pill opened blank — but it still
   overlaid its neighbours. In flow, neither fault can recur.)

   Reduced motion is handled by the global clamp at the top of this file,
   which zeroes transition-duration and -delay on every element. */
.plb-icobtn{position:relative;isolation:isolate;min-width:36px;padding-inline:10px;justify-content:center;gap:0}
.plb-icobtn:hover,.plb-icobtn:focus-visible,.plb-icobtn[aria-expanded="true"]{z-index:4}
.plb-icobtn .plb-lbl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0fr;align-items:center;min-width:0;padding-left:0;opacity:0;color:inherit;transition:grid-template-columns var(--dur-3) var(--ease-entrance),padding-left var(--dur-3) var(--ease-entrance),opacity var(--dur-2) var(--ease-standard)}
.plb-icobtn .plb-lbl-i{overflow:hidden;min-width:0;white-space:nowrap}
.plb-icobtn:hover .plb-lbl,.plb-icobtn:focus-visible .plb-lbl,.plb-icobtn[aria-expanded="true"] .plb-lbl{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-left:7px;opacity:1}

/* Thin separator between a menu's stacked sections (Save vs. Share & export). */
